note Translated from cpython Lib/_pydatetime.py, datetime.replace.
note Return a new datetime with new values for the specified fields.

note GAP: tzinfo is an abstract base class that user code subclasses (utcoffset, dst, tzname); the doc has no interface or trait, so it is left opaque
type TzInfo

type Datetime
    field year as an Int
    field month as an Int
    field day as an Int
    field hour as an Int
    field minute as an Int
    field second as an Int
    field microsecond as an Int
    field tzinfo as a maybe TzInfo
    field fold as an Int

note The constructor checks every field's range (and that fold is 0 or 1) and fails if one is out of range.
to new_datetime year and month and day and hour and minute and second and microsecond and tzinfo and fold
    given year is an Int
    given month is an Int
    given day is an Int
    given hour is an Int
    given minute is an Int
    given second is an Int
    given microsecond is an Int
    given tzinfo is a maybe TzInfo
    given fold is an Int
    produces a Datetime
    fails with ValueError, TypeError

note WORKAROUND: Python uses True as a third value for tzinfo, because None already means "no time zone". Keep versus replace-with-a-maybe needs its own choice type.
choice TzinfoChange
    Keep
    Replace with new_tzinfo as a maybe TzInfo

note GAP: objects, methods and self - replace is a method called as dt.replace(...); here self is an ordinary first parameter
note UNCLEAR: the doc never shows an operation with more than four parameters; `and` between parameter names is borrowed from `a Dashboard from profile and orders and alerts`
to replace self with year and month and day and hour and minute and second and microsecond and tzinfo and fold
    given self is a Datetime
    note GAP: default and keyword-only arguments - every argument defaults to None (tzinfo to True) and fold is keyword-only; Scribe callers must pass all nine, writing nothing or Keep for each field they do not change
    given year is a maybe Int
    given month is a maybe Int
    given day is a maybe Int
    given hour is a maybe Int
    given minute is a maybe Int
    given second is a maybe Int
    given microsecond is a maybe Int
    given tzinfo is a TzinfoChange
    given fold is a maybe Int
    note GAP: interfaces and dynamic dispatch - Python returns type(self), so a subclass of datetime gets an instance of that subclass back; Scribe can only promise the declared type
    produces a Datetime
    fails with ValueError, TypeError

    note WORKAROUND: no "value or default" expression for a maybe, and choose is a statement, so each field is a var set in both branches. Nine Python two-line ifs become nine six-line blocks.
    var new_year starts at year of self
    choose year
        when some given_year
            set new_year to given_year
        when nothing
            set new_year to year of self
    var new_month starts at month of self
    choose month
        when some given_month
            set new_month to given_month
        when nothing
            set new_month to month of self
    var new_day starts at day of self
    choose day
        when some given_day
            set new_day to given_day
        when nothing
            set new_day to day of self
    var new_hour starts at hour of self
    choose hour
        when some given_hour
            set new_hour to given_hour
        when nothing
            set new_hour to hour of self
    var new_minute starts at minute of self
    choose minute
        when some given_minute
            set new_minute to given_minute
        when nothing
            set new_minute to minute of self
    var new_second starts at second of self
    choose second
        when some given_second
            set new_second to given_second
        when nothing
            set new_second to second of self
    var new_microsecond starts at microsecond of self
    choose microsecond
        when some given_microsecond
            set new_microsecond to given_microsecond
        when nothing
            set new_microsecond to microsecond of self
    var new_tzinfo starts at tzinfo of self
    choose tzinfo
        when Keep
            set new_tzinfo to tzinfo of self
        when Replace with new_tzinfo_value
            set new_tzinfo to new_tzinfo_value
    note UNCLEAR: example 5 binds a payload by its field name (`when Circle with radius`); renaming it here (new_tzinfo_value for new_tzinfo) is not shown, and binding the field name would clash with the var
    var new_fold starts at fold of self
    choose fold
        when some given_fold
            set new_fold to given_fold
        when nothing
            set new_fold to fold of self
    give back try new_datetime new_year and new_month and new_day and new_hour and new_minute and new_second and new_microsecond and new_tzinfo and new_fold
